
How to set up the server
------------------------

1. Create a Python environment (this step is optional)
My preferred tool to manage Python environments is conda-forge.
First, install conda by running the Miniforge installer
(see https://conda-forge.org).
Then, create and activate an environment for the cgos server:
conda create -n cgos-server python==3.12.0
conda activate cgos-server

2. Go to directory <server-code>
cd <server-code>

3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Configure cgos19.yaml
You have to decide where on the server the data of the running
program should be written. I will refer to this directory as
<server-data>.
You must as well decide where on the server the web pages of
the server should be stored. I will refer to this directory as
<server-html>.
Edit configs/generic/cgos19.yaml and replace all occurrences of
<server-data> with your path for <server-data>. Do the same with
<server-html>. These paths may be either absolute or relative to
the current working directory that is in effect when the server
will be started.
Note 1: <server-html> should be a directory that your web server
presents to client browsers. In my case (Ubuntu 24.04), the web
server is Apache2, configured to use /var/www/html as its base
directory. Thus, <server-html> is /var/www/html/cgos on the
machine running the server, accessible from the outside by its
URL http://<server-name>/cgos. Don't forget to change owner and
group of this directory to those of <server-code>, so that the
server can write the WEB pages to the directory, for example:
sudo mkdir -p /var/www/html/cgos
cd /var/www/html
sudo chown <owner>:<group> cgos
sudo chmod 755 cgos
Note 2: If you have installed a firewall on the server machine,
you must open up the three ports on which your server is going
to listen for TCP connections, for example:
sudo ufw allow 6809/tcp
sudo ufw allow 6813/tcp
sudo ufw allow 6819/tcp

5. Start the Go server
python cgos/server.py <path_to_your_config_file> &
Note: In my case, the config file is configs/examples/cgos19.yaml

6. Start the webpage builder
python cgos/webuild.py <path_to_your_config_file> &
Note: The config file here is the exact same file as in 5. above.

7. Stop the Go server
cp killfiles/kill_cgos19 <server-code>
The contents of the killfile are ignored, only its presence counts.
It is automatically deleted when the server is started again.

8. Stop the webpage builder
cp killfiles/kill_webuild19 <server-code>
The contents of the killfile are ignored, only its presence counts.
It is automatically deleted when the builder is started again.

